    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Burning on passing urine and going often for two days. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Hatshepsut called this morning and was seen the same day. For two days she has had burning when passing urine, urgency and frequency, with lower abdominal discomfort. She has no fever, chills, back or flank pain, nausea or vomiting, and no vaginal discharge or itching. She has had one bladder infection before, years ago. She is eating and drinking normally. She has taken semaglutide 0.25 mg weekly for four weeks with mild fullness after large meals and is due to step up to 0.5 mg this week. She takes metformin 1000 mg and atorvastatin each evening. Her glucose readings at home have been 110 to 140 mg/dL. Her extraction site has healed. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Dysuria, urgency, frequency and suprapubic discomfort; no fever or flank pain</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Type 2 diabetes on metformin and semaglutide; no SGLT2 inhibitor</td></tr><tr><td>Urine dipstick</td><td>Leukocyte esterase and nitrite positive; no blood; glucose negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
